      "message": "Thanks for the review, Julia. PS2 makes these changes:\n\n1. Duplicate cache: OneLineShaper::fFallbackFonts and OneLineShaper::FontKey are removed. matchResolvedFonts() calls defaultFallback() directly. Now there is one lookup per miss, and the key includes families[0]. Thus the result in a paragraph no longer depends on the order of the styles. VariationCache continues to own the clones, so the uniqueID check in alreadyTriedTypefaces does not change.\n\n2. Size: FallbackCache is now an SkLRUCache (the same as ParagraphCache) with a limit of 4096 entries. An entry uses about 100 bytes, so a full cache uses about 400 KB. I counted font manager queries for 5000 paragraphs of random CJK text (15000 lookups):\n\n   | ideograph pool | no cache | cap 1024 | cap 2048 | cap 4096 | no limit |\n   |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   | 400  | 15000 | 481  | 481  | 481  | 481  |\n   | 2000 | 15000 | 3003 | 1916 | 1916 | 1916 |\n   | 5000 | 15000 | 4250 | 3607 | 3280 | 3280 |\n\n   2048 is just enough for the 2000 pool (about 2100 keys), so I used 4096. 4096 gives the same result as no limit for all three pools. The new test SkParagraph_FallbackCacheIsBounded queries 65536 PUA codepoints and makes sure that the oldest entry is removed.\n\n   Note: an LRU hit also changes the cache (find() moves the entry to the front). Thus a FontCollection that is shared across threads now also writes on a hit. FontCollection does not use locks before or after this CL, and FaceCache also writes on a miss. If you prefer a cache that only reads on a hit, I can change it to a THashMap that resets when it is full.\n\n3. Hasher: it now uses SkGoodHash for the SkString fields and for the full SkFontStyle, so it does not allocate and it agrees with operator\u003d\u003d.\n\nBase: the CL is now on main, and it does not depend on 1396956. Without 1396956, clearCaches() clears the fallback cache. The setters that change the font managers (setAssetFontManager(), setDynamicFontManager(), setTestFontManager(), setDefaultFontManager()) and enableFontFallback() / disableFontFallback() also clear it. When 1396956 lands, I can move this to resetResolutionCaches().\n\nNumbers (CoreText, macOS, release dm, 1000 new paragraphs on one FontCollection, median of 7 interleaved rounds, us/paragraph):\n\n| | main | CL |\n|---|---|---|\n| first 500 | 75.4 | 45.7 |\n| next 500 | 55.4 | 18.4 |\n\nAll SkParagraph tests pass on macOS with and without --nativeFonts. Both new tests fail without the change to FontCollection. I did not run the tests on Linux / fontconfig.",
